Fillets: a walk cut before a singular section past its spine's end ends
there (mitcad#343).

The case: a rounding of radius 0.5 on three pieces of the edge between a
large torus and a plane that a rod of the solid interrupts. Past a piece's
end the contact on the plane runs onto a torus of radius 0.6 that wraps
the rod's foot; there the contact speeds up from 1.25 to 20.5 along the
guide, and patch 0077's ChFi3d_CutSingularExtension cuts the line at
18.0021 (the spine 17.92 long), before the singular sections. The cut end
lies on no arc, so ComputeData left the end open (intl 0) and the loop of
PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine, finding the line short of the guide's end, took
the walk up again from the cut, into the same sections; the corners at the
pieces' ends then failed.

ChFi3d_CutSingularExtension now returns the ends it cut, and ComputeData
closes such an end (intl or intf 1 where it was 0): the cut end is the
blend's end for the corner, as where a contact reaches the edge of its
face. The common points the data took at the walk's end are kept: a corner
elsewhere (the rounding along an arc of a cylinder's top cut by two
planes, its walk past the end cut there) builds from them. With patch 0933
the design's replayed rounding, the three pieces and the edges of the rod
between them, builds in every order of its contours within 0.0032 mm3 of
the file's change (7.5193 mm3); before, a corner failed.

Upstream: new.
